Suggests: classicube-data (>= ${source:Upstream-Version})
Description: ClassiCube block building game
 A Minecraft Classic compatible game (SDL3 window and gamepad, desktop GL 1, OpenAL).
 /usr/games/classicube runs it from a per-user directory (~/.local/share/classicube), where it
 keeps options, maps and screenshots. It does not contain Mojang's textures, sounds and music:
 the game's launcher downloads them on first run, or classicube-data (our LAN repository only)
 installs them. See /usr/share/doc/classicube/README.Debian.

# Mojang's textures and audio: licensed content we may not redistribute (Section local/*), so
# tools/repo-publish.sh puts it in the ps3-licensed suite, never in ps3 or ps3-dev. Until
# 1.3.8~git20261014.aa47929-1+ps3.366 these files were in the classicube package itself.
Package: classicube-data
Architecture: all
Section: local/games
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: classicube (<< 1.3.8~git20261014.aa47929-1+ps3.366~)
Replaces: classicube (<< 1.3.8~git20261014.aa47929-1+ps3.366~)
Description: ClassiCube's textures, sounds and music (Mojang's Minecraft Classic assets)
 The default texture pack (static.classicube.net/default.zip: the Minecraft Classic textures
 from Mojang's client jars, with ClassiCube's patches), the sounds as 16-bit WAVs and the music,
 fetched from Mojang's resource server as the game's launcher would. Not redistributable: our
 LAN repository only.
